    "body": "Claim released. The time budget of the worker ended before the gate was green.\n\nHeld work: branch `issue/2004-top-z-level` (commit d802f493a), draft PR #2013 (`Refs #2004`).\n\nDone:\n\n- The shared level law `cut_levels` starts at `top - stepdown`. The app's `ladder_planes` calls it.\n- Circular vault inner rings keep their opening plane. The turning face drops a rung on the top of the work.\n- The audit of all depth-stepping operations is in the PR body.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/2004-top-z-level.md`.\n- Follow-up #2012: remainder last step against equal steps.\n\nLeft:\n\n- About 40 motion tests fail. They expect a level at Top Z. The PR body lists the count per binary.\n- Read these tests with care, because they are gouge or solid laws: `blind_floor::a_blind_pocket_never_enters_solid_under_any_ladder`, `machining3d::random_ladders_never_walk_a_ring_into_hanging_or_floor_solid`, `machining3d::a_prev_mask_only_ever_removes_cuts`, `machining3d::degenerate_input_refuses_cleanly`.\n- Run the motion binaries after `radial_step`, including the new `top_z_level`.\n- Run the app suites. Regenerate the goldens of the changed operations (`golden_cl`, `solid_law_goldens` and the other goldens). No golden is regenerated yet.\n- Run clippy.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
