    "body": "Round 4 result on `issue/2004-top-z-level`, head `44ebc51dd1e6d5807af4f49237c66f49ce284f6e` (PR #2013, draft).\n\n- Rotary: the new refusal in `rotary_offset` is correct. The windows v 0 to 8 and v 19 to 28 held only air under the wrap top (rho 2.5). The old program cut only air there. The test pins the two windows as refusals by name. Decision item 8.\n- Code defects found in round 4: none. No check is loosened.\n- Each red motion fixture of round 3 is changed. Each old expectation counted the Top Z air level. The PR body lists each change with its reason.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --no-fail-fast`: green except `vertical_arc_entry`. Its 3 tests now fail only at the recording guard: `crates/post/tests/recorded/inputs/vertical_arc_{x,y,oblique}.cl` are stale.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nRemaining:\n1. Regenerate the three `vertical_arc_*.cl` recordings (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test vertical_arc_entry`), then run post's `vertical_arc_entry`.\n2. Run the app suites, with the `area.rs` unit test `ladder_planes_match_the_level_law_and_never_hang`.\n3. Regenerate and read the goldens `golden_cl` and `solid_law_goldens`.\n4. Trace and trochoidal slot do not read the material top. A Top Z under the stock top gives them a first bite deeper than one stepdown. This needs `material_top` from the app (`generate.rs`).\n\nI release the claim. The worktree is removed. The branch holds the work.\n",
