    "body": "Round 5 result on `issue/2004-top-z-level`, head `b18b928131467a963022f3efcd6bc6352fd07599` (PR #2013, draft).\n\n- Trace, engrave and trochoidal slot now read the material top. `TraceParams` and `TrochoidParams` get `material_top`, and `generate.rs` fills it from the stock top. With Top Z under the stock top, the first level stays at Top Z. No first cut is deeper than one stepdown. Decision item 9.\n- Pins: `top_z_level::a_trace_under_stock_over_top_z_keeps_the_level_at_top_z` and `top_z_level::a_trochoidal_slot_under_stock_over_top_z_keeps_the_level_at_top_z` (motion). `top_z_stock_over` (app, 2 tests, levels `[18, 15, 12]` on a stock top of 20).\n- The three `vertical_arc_{x,y,oblique}.cl` recordings are regenerated. Each diff loses only the air level at Top Z. The post `vertical_arc_entry` test now counts two arc blocks (levels Z -2 and Z -4). The PR body lists the posted change.\n- App: `ladder_planes_match_the_level_law_and_never_hang` and the named trace, engrave and trochoid binaries are green. Clippy on `camcraft-motion`, `camcraft-post` and `camcraft-app` is clean.\n- No gouge, verify, load or solid check is loosened.\n\nRemaining:\n1. Regenerate and read the goldens. `golden_cl` has 12 red tests and `solid_law_goldens` has 4 red tests. Each read diff loses the level at Top Z 0. The PR body lists them by name.\n2. In `solid_law_goldens::a_lead_on_the_rings_own_circle_is_refused`, change the expected crossing list from 6 to 4 entries (the third level is gone). The refusal stays.\n3. Run the full app suites that the change touches, not only the named filters.\n4. Then change `Refs #2004` to `Fixes #2004` and make the PR ready for review.\n\nI release the claim. The worktree is removed. The branch holds the work.\n",
